  "analytic_proof": "For p odd, h=sum_(s,a,b) q_(s,a,b)^p q_(s+1,a,b), r0=r1=2. Site0: N height1 columns with I=1 and one height2 column with I(1)=1,I(2)=2. Site1: i height1 columns with I=1. T={0}. Let F=p^-i h^i (Z_(0,1,1))^(N+1-pi)*Z_(0,2,2). The target X monomial X_(0,1,1)^(N+1) X_(0,2,2) X_(1,1,1)^i in J_F has exact coefficient (N+1)! i! /p^i; other determinant branch vanishes by Z multidegree. v=vp(N!)+vp(i!)-i. Delta2-Delta1=ell(N)+4+3ell(i), and dQ2-dQ1=2, so B2=B1-(ell(N)+4+3ell(i)-2/(p^2-1)) < B1. The previous universally proven 1x1 slack ensures v>B2 for all odd p,k,i. This checks an honest size-2 determinant but a tightly controlled F and X coefficient, NOT arbitrary high-rank minors or global theta class membership."
